 "summary": "There is no single procedure: the FCOM SOP lists what to do under Management of Degraded Navigation, and the crew reviews it in the arrival briefing. This brief leads with RNAV(GNSS) approaches with LNAV/VNAV minima; RNAV(RNP) rules are kept for reference under From the manuals. A loss on one side only: continue on the remaining AP/FD. A loss on both sides, XTK above 0.3 NM or 75 ft below the path: discontinue unless visual references are enough to proceed visually. Hand-flying needs the FD: in approach, AP and FD both off is not authorized without F-LOC deviation.",
